04:53:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-plans-for-major-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-in-greenland/a-79656889--25eef0012d41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-plans-for-major-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-in-greenland/a-79656889?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president has claimed Greenland holds vast and easily accessible oil reserves without providing evidence or details. His announcement follows a deal expanding the US military presence on the Arctic island.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading graph about alleged Russian bot activity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a90a665efba2e5d02eadf968fdc314e9589a546ba7caafb30738299321ef6e00</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-graph-about-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769--ec259de6b65a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-graph-about-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Did attacks on Russian data centers reduce bot activity around Germany's AfD? A viral graph claims they did. But it contains significant inconsistencies and provides no evidence to support the claim.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Do non-German nationals commit more crimes than Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b409965364b59433a9e52a13eea17eb7a634a330e0ccfb9dda6c249957658639</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:53:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/do-non-german-nationals-commit-more-crimes-than-germans/a-79657273--07f237eb177a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/do-non-german-nationals-commit-more-crimes-than-germans/a-79657273?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">People without German passports appear more frequently in German police crime statistics than German nationals. A new study explains why.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
